From 1ec193b63b964378c90932a5879d8756d0f93256 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:46:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] One stretch for the reservations, carved from its middle;
 larger commits only without a pool (#2873)

Four regions, one for each set of mmap flags and each carved from its
start, put a small unit's arenas under seven of the kernel's
third-level page tables where their own mappings had been under three,
and every exit and unmap scans those: 24,000 kernel cycles a unit more
in unmap_page_range and free_pgd_range on the 9700X, a third of what the
fewer calls saved. Now one stretch of 16 TiB, whose halves are carved
from the middle: the upper one for the mappings that take huge pages,
advised once, whole; the lower one for those mapped base pages
throughout and the tables'. Both are MAP_NORESERVE, which changes
nothing where commit is charged.

On a thread with a pool, a commit takes what it took before. The pool
keeps its arenas' commits, so they are few, and its releases discard
each arena's pages, which frees the page tables of every whole 2 MB
they cover: with larger commits each unit of musl's as one command
built them again, 37,000 kernel cycles a unit (+5.0%).

A hello.c compile here: 5 mmap, 35 mprotect and 7 madvise calls where
it made 36, 51 and 10; the same object.

Part of #2873.

